    "type": "WSI",
    "diagnosis": "Proliferative verrucous leukoplakia",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Bulky, hyperkeratotic epithelial proliferation (not reactive). The epithelium exhibits strikingly broad, blunt, cumbrous rete ridges, with less impressive surface keratinization. Occasional keratin pearls and dyskeratosis are noted, but cytological atypia is minimal and confined to the basalmost region. A dense lichenoid lymphocytic infiltrate occupies the lamina propria in intimate relationship with the bases of the rete ridges.",
    "source": "Sarah G. Fitzpatrick",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/26765.dzi",
    "thumbnail": null
  }
